WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.180
Welcome to Strategic Service Management. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Manage the service portfolio in line with needs and organizational capabilities.

2
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:21.830
Consider this scenario. A company launches three offers without checking operating capacity. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:32.070
Start with two steps: Analyze needs and market demand. Then Define the service portfolio. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:41.910
Continue with Align capacity and capabilities. Then Review service value and fit. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:41.910 --> 00:01:03.120
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous service catalog, demand forecast, portfolio decisions tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: adding services without validating demand, cost and capability; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:17.370
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
